    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e77fd30b_b1c88418",
        "filename": "include/private/SkHdrMetadata.h",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 41,
      "author": {
        "id": 8704
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-09-10T21:23:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This LGTM, but I don\u0027t understand why this is needed for the Rust PNG integration, which exposes pre-parsed data (two `u32`s rather than a sequence of bytes).  See https://docs.rs/png/latest/png/struct.ContentLightLevelInfo.html\n\nSame question for `serialize`, `parsePngChunk`, and `serializePngChunk`.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 41,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 41,
        "endChar": 35
      },
      "revId": "f5d471106806bb8132348ee4e72824677b20d822",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "2c382e0d_59d518c6",
        "filename": "include/private/SkHdrMetadata.h",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 41,
      "author": {
        "id": 6225
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-09-11T13:32:07Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The non-Rust PNG interface doesn\u0027t parse the CLLI/MDCV chunks, so we need to parse them ourselves. Simiarly, `serializePngChunk` for non-Rust PNG encoding.\n\nThe other `serialize` and `parse` functions are intended to replace the many parsing functions sprinkled throughout Chrome (e.g, [here](https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:ui/gfx/hdr_metadata_mac.mm;l\u003d16;drc\u003dacf33dd703904a799feffd313152337c95e113bf), [here](https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:media/parsers/h264_parser.cc;l\u003d1571;drc\u003d48d6f7175422b2c969c14258f9f8d5b196c28d18), etc).",
      "parentUuid": "e77fd30b_b1c88418",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 41,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 41,
        "endChar": 35
      },
      "revId": "f5d471106806bb8132348ee4e72824677b20d822",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "daab4d22_ca7fd27c",
        "filename": "include/private/SkHdrMetadata.h",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 41,
      "author": {
        "id": 8704
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-09-11T15:40:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e The non-Rust PNG interface doesn\u0027t parse the CLLI/MDCV chunks, so we need to parse them ourselves. Simiarly, `serializePngChunk` for non-Rust PNG encoding.\n\nI see.  This may be okay, but I want to point out that `serializePngChunk` doesn\u0027t seem **immediately** necessary:\n\n* IIUC the legacy `blink::PNGImageDecoder` would only **deserialize** the CLLI/MCDV chunks.  From that perspective, preserving the legacy functionality doesn\u0027t really need `serializePngChunk`.\n* Additionally both `SkPngEncoder` and `SkPngRustEncoder` discover the color profile (of the image being serialized) using `SkPixmap::colorSpace` / `SkColorSpace`.  Does that API provide a way to read the HDR metadata for CLLI/MCDV chunks?\n\n\u003e The other `serialize` and `parse` functions are intended to replace the many parsing functions sprinkled throughout Chrome (e.g, [here](https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:ui/gfx/hdr_metadata_mac.mm;l\u003d16;drc\u003dacf33dd703904a799feffd313152337c95e113bf), [here](https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:media/parsers/h264_parser.cc;l\u003d1571;drc\u003d48d6f7175422b2c969c14258f9f8d5b196c28d18), etc).\n\nAck.  I agree that such deduplication is desirable.",
      "parentUuid": "2c382e0d_59d518c6",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 41,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 41,
        "endChar": 35
      },
      "revId": "f5d471106806bb8132348ee4e72824677b20d822",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
